Kreative Studio pose editor, animation part (STU-PE2). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no build step. The same file runs in Node 22 (CommonJS require) and in the browser (classic <script>, no modules). Use exactly this wrapper and nothing outside it:

(function () {
  'use strict';
  const NS = typeof module === 'object' && module.exports ? null : (globalThis.KKPose = globalThis.KKPose || {});
  const need = (name, file) => (NS ? NS[name] : require(file));
  // ... the code; get other pose modules with need('vec', './vec.js') INSIDE functions (load order in the browser is free) ...
  const api = { /* exported names */ };
  if (NS) NS.<NAME> = api; else module.exports = api;
})();

Angles are degrees in every API. Coordinates are metres: +X is the figure's left, -Y its front, +Z up. Matrices are arrays of 9 numbers, row-major. Do not change the test file.

Write tools/anim-cli.js for Kreative Studio (Node 22, CommonJS): clips from saved poses and their exports without the browser, for Claude and local models (STU-PE2). Model it on tools/pose-cli.js (same main(argv, io) shape, same error style). Do not change the test file.

Requires: fs, path, zlib is not needed; A = require('../public/js/pose/anim.js') (newClip, setKey, sample), and from require('../lib/anim-api.js'): checkClip(clip) (throws with a message), checkView(view), render(clip, format, {hands, view}) -> {body, type, ext} where body is a Buffer, or a plain object for 'frames'.

main(argv, io = {out: (s) => process.stdout.write(s), err: (s) => process.stderr.write(s)}) returns the exit code; any thrown error -> io.err('error: ' + message + '\n') and return 1.
Flags (each value flag takes the next argument): --clip FILE, --poses FILE,FILE,..., --times T,T,..., --fps N, --length S, --ease NAME, --loop, --no-loop, --out FILE, --hands, --width N, --height N, --yaw DEG, --pitch DEG, --cols N, --sample T. Any other flag: throw new Error('unknown flag ' + flag).
- --clip: the clip is JSON.parse of the file.
- --poses: read each file; a file whose JSON has a .pose uses that (a saved pose's meta.json), else the JSON itself is the pose. clip = A.newClip({fps: Number(--fps) or 24, length: Number(--length) or 1, loop: !--no-loop}). Times: --times split on ',' as numbers (when given its count must equal the pose count, else throw new Error('--times needs one time per pose')); else evenly spaced: loop: i * length / n; not loop: n === 1 ? 0 : i * length / (n - 1). Add each pose with A.setKey(clip, t, pose, --ease or 'ease-in-out').
- Neither: throw new Error('give --clip FILE or --poses FILE,FILE,...').
- c = checkClip(clip).
- --sample T: io.out(JSON.stringify(A.sample(c, Number(T)), null, 2) + '\n'); return 0.
- --out FILE: format by extension: .bvh -> 'bvh', .glb -> 'glb', .png -> 'strip', .json -> 'frames'; any other: throw new Error('--out must end in .bvh, .glb, .png or .json'). view = checkView({width, height, yaw, pitch, cols} with only the flags given, as numbers). r = render(c, format, {hands: has --hands, view}); write r.body (objects as JSON with 2 spaces) to FILE (make its folder first, recursive); io.err('wrote ' + FILE + '\n'); return 0.
- Else print the clip: io.out(JSON.stringify(c, null, 2) + '\n'); return 0.
At the end: module.exports = {main}; if (require.main === module) process.exitCode = main(process.argv.slice(2)).
